# Normalize every tracked file to LF in the repository. All 1160 tracked files
# are text (verified 2026-08-04: `git grep -I` matches every one of them, and
# the only binaries here — the per-platform plugin binaries — are gitignored,
# see .gitignore:34-37), so there is nothing for text=auto to misdetect.
#
# Without this, a CRLF-writing tool can convert tracked files in place and the
# conversion is invisible to review: measured 2026-08-04, 72 tracked files were
# CRLF-ified with ZERO content change (`git diff --ignore-cr-at-eol` reported no
# hunks for any of them), so `git status` showed 72 "modified" files that were
# byte-identical modulo \r. That noise both hides real edits and gets committed
# verbatim by any `git add -A`.
* text=auto

# Force LF for scripts that are exec'd directly via their shebang line.
# A CRLF shebang (`#!/bin/sh\r`) is read as an interpreter path literally
# ending in \r, which does not exist, so exec fails outright — this is not a
# style preference, it is the difference between a hook running and not
# running at all.
#
# Measured (2026-08-03): with core.autocrlf=true (a common Windows git
# default/installer default) and no .gitattributes, a checkout of this repo
# converts .githooks/* to CRLF on disk even though the committed blobs are
# LF-only. Every `git commit` then fails with
# "fatal: cannot exec '.githooks/pre-commit': No such file or directory"
# under strict POSIX exec (confirmed on WSL2); the gate does not silently
# allow the commit through — it blocks all commits outright, so this is a
# total-breakage bug, not a fail-open.
.githooks/* text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

# The plugin launcher dispatchers are shell scripts with NO .sh extension
# (crates/<name>/bin/<name>), so the *.sh rule above never covered them.
# Measured (2026-08-04): crates/ctxrot/bin/ctxrot was the one launcher of 39
# that got CRLF-ified, and every invocation then died with
# "cannot execute: required file not found" (exec resolving the interpreter as
# `/bin/sh\r`), rc=127 — which took the ctxrot Stop/PostToolUse hooks out of
# service. Note rc=127 is NOT the fail-closed path that
# crates/ctxrot/tests/launcher_missing_binary.rs pins: the launcher never ran
# at all, so none of its own protocol-aware handling applied.
crates/*/bin/* text eol=lf

# ...but the per-platform binaries staged next to those dispatchers are ELF,
# not text. They are gitignored today, so this only matters if one is ever
# force-added — keep eol conversion off them regardless. In .gitattributes the
# LAST matching pattern wins, so these must stay below the rule above.
crates/*/bin/*-linux-x86_64 binary
crates/*/bin/*-linux-arm64 binary
crates/*/bin/*-darwin-x86_64 binary
crates/*/bin/*-darwin-arm64 binary
crates/*/bin/*-windows-x86_64.exe binary
